{
  "action": "In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.",
  "cves": [
    "CVE-2026-10650",
    "CVE-2026-78161"
  ],
  "description": "It was discovered that Libwebsockets incorrectly handled certain SSH\nprotocol messages in its SSH protocol handler. A remote attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause Libwebsockets to consume excessive\nresources, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-10650)\n\nIt was discovered that Libwebsockets incorrectly handled certain malformed\nCBOR data. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause\nLibwebsockets to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or execute\narbitrary code. This issue only affected Ubuntu 24.04 LTS and Ubuntu 26.04\nLTS. (CVE-2026-78161)",
  "id": "USN-8822-1",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in Libwebsockets.",
